<title>TAIWAN: Moderate earthquake rocks Taiwan.</title>
<headline>Moderate earthquake rocks Taiwan.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>A moderate earthquake measuring 5.0 on the Richter scale struck central and eastern Taiwan on Wednesday, but police said there were no reports of injuries or serious damage.</p>
<p>The Central Weather Bureau said that the epicentre of the tremor was 19.1 kms (11.87 miles) northeast of Taiwan's central Ali mountain and some 10.6 kms (6.59 miles) beneath the earth's surface.</p>
<p>The earthquake was felt in parts of central and eastern Taiwan, the weather bureau said.</p>
